    "evidence_text": "Pardon Mon Affaire\n\nPardon Mon Affaire (French: Un \u00e9l\u00e9phant \u00e7a trompe \u00e9norm\u00e9ment , English: \"An Elephant Can Be Extremely Deceptive\" ) is a 1976 French comedy film co-written and directed by Yves Robert.\n\n It was remade as the 1984 American film \"The Woman in Red\".\n\nElephant (2003 film)\n\nElephant is a 2003 drama film edited, written and directed by Gus Van Sant.\n\n2003 Cannes Film Festival\n\nThe 56th Cannes Film Festival started on 14 May and ran until 25 May 2003.\n\n French opera and theatre director, filmmaker, actor and producer Patrice Ch\u00e9reau was the President of the Jury.\n\n The Palme d'Or went to the American film \"Elephant\" by Gus Van Sant based on the Columbine High School massacre.\n\nWhispers: An Elephant's Tale\n\nWhispers: An Elephant's Tale is a 2000 American film, starring Angela Bassett, Joanna Lumley, Anne Archer, Debi Derryberry and Kevin Michael Richardson.\n\n It was co-written, co-produced and directed by Dereck Joubert.",
